  "raw_output": "{\n  \"exercis_typ\": \"CEFR Englis_English Placement Test\",\n  \"section_id\": 5,\n  \"section_title\": \"Reading Comprehension\",\n  \"cefr_range\": \"B2-C1\",\n  \"reading_text\": \"\\\\\nIn the bustling city of New York, traffic congestion has become a pressing issue. As more people move into urban areas and vehicles multiply, traditional roads cannot accommodate all the flow of cars. This problem has led to innovative solutions such as elevated highways, underground tunnels, or even bike lanes designed specifically for pedestrians and cyclists.\\\\\nThe city government is considering implementing a new policy that encourages the use of public transportation by providing incentives like discounted fares or free rides during peak hours. This move has garnered mixed reactions from residents, with some supporting it as a way to reduce pollution and improve traffic flow while others fear that such measures may discourage car ownership and hinder mobility.\\\\\nThe rise of smart technology is also playing a role in revolutionizing the way people navigate city streets. Apps like Waze and Google Maps have become essential tools for planning routes, finding parking spots, or even sharing rides with strangers through platforms like Uber and Lyft.\\\\\nAlthough these innovations offer solutions to some traffic challenges, they also raise new questions about privacy concerns when data is collected for optimizing routes or predicting future travel patterns.\\\\\nOverall, the efforts to manage traffic in New York City reflect a broader global trend towards finding balance between urban development and environmental sustainability.\"\n},\n\"questions\": [\n  {\n    \"question_number\": 36,\n    \"question\": \"What is the main concern mentioned in the passage?\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"A. The rise of smart technology\",\n      \"B. Traffic congestion in New York City\",\n      \"C. Increasing car ownership rates\",\n      \"D. Lack of public transportation infrastructure\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"B\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"question_number\": 37,\n    \"question\": \"Which of the following is NOT a solution being considered by the city government to address traffic problems?\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"A. Implementing discounted public transportation fares\",\n      \"B. Building elevated highways and underground tunnels\",\n      \"C. Encouraging the use of private cars\",\n      \"D. Creating bike lanes for pedestrians and cyclists\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"C\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"question_number\": 38,\n    \"question\": \"What is the author's tone towards the new policy promoting public transportation?\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"A. Neutral\",\n      \"B. Positive\",\n      \"C. Critical\",\n      \"D. Optimistic\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"A\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"question_number\": 39,\n    \"question\": \"Which of the following best describes the author's view on smart technology used for traffic management?\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"A. The author believes it is unhelpful\",\n      \"B. The author sees both benefits and drawbacks\",\n      \"C. The author thinks it is the only solution\",\n      \"D. The author believes it will completely replace human decision-making\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"B\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"question_number\": 40,\n    \"question\": \"What is the author's main purpose in writing this passage?\",\n    \"options\": [\n      \"A. To promote a specific transportation mode\",\n      \"B. To explain how smart technology is helping with traffic\",\n      \"C. To discuss the challenges and potential solutions to traffic congestion in New York City\",\n      \"D. To criticize the city government's policies\"\n    ],\n    \"answer\": \"C\"\n  }\n]\n}",
